#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Regenerate the release-candidate results in the pinned container.

Usage: contrib/regenerate-rc SWAYWARD_SHA [--dry-run] [--image NAME] [--shards N]
                             [--trial I3_FILE ...]

This is the T4 runbook in one command. Run it on the host from a clean oracle
checkout. It never commits and never pushes; review and commit the changed
files afterwards. Steps, in this order:

1. Pin: set the swayward pin and snapshot name to SWAYWARD_SHA, and rename the
   swayward result, classification and pending.toml entries to the new name.
2. Image: build the oracle image from pins.toml, unless an image with the same
   pins.toml already exists.
3. Units, one at a time, each container capped at 4 GiB with swap disabled:
   - i3-derived-capture: record sway's commands from the i3 suite, recapture
     sway-ipc/i3-derived from pinned sway, and require two sway replays of the
     new corpus that match on every row.
   - i3-suite/sway: two serial `--shard 1/1` runs.
   - i3-suite/swayward: two complete runs, each as N parallel shards.
   - sway-ipc/COMPOSITOR/CORPUS: two runs each, for every pins.toml snapshot
     compositor (i3, sway, swayward, then the others in pins.toml order).
     SwayFX units get the host's DRM render node (--device /dev/dri/renderD128):
     SwayFX renders only through GLES2, and software rendering crashes.
   The units are every result in pending.toml plus every swayward result.
   Two runs agree when their results are equal apart from the `date` line. For
   sway-IPC state and events, rows pair by (scenario, request, occurrence),
   and for random by seed;
   rows that differ, or are unstable in either run, install from run1 as
   unstable with recounted [run] counts and are listed in evidence.log. sway
   (the reference) disagreeing on any row, more than 5% of rows disagreeing,
   or any other [run] or row-set difference fails the unit. For
   the i3 suite, assertions listed in i3/unstable.toml and files listed in
   i3/flaky.toml are excluded, and both runs must pass every canary. An
   agreeing unit installs the first run as the committed result and drops its
   pending.toml entry. A disagreeing unit stops the run and installs nothing.
4. Finish: regenerate the docs/results.md generated regions and run contrib/validate.

Each unit appends one evidence line (unit, runs, wall time, agreement, diff
lines against the committed result) to target/rc/SHA8/evidence.log. A rerun
skips units that already have an agreeing line for the same oracle commit,
swayward commit and image. `--dry-run` changes nothing: it checks the
prerequisites and prints the full unit plan with the exact commands.

`--trial I3_FILE` (repeatable) rehearses only the i3-derived-capture unit,
recording just those i3 test files. It runs the same steps and checks but
installs no result, leaves pending.toml alone, skips the finish, and logs to
target/rc/SHA8-trial/, so a trial never satisfies the real unit on resume.
The trial still recaptures sway-ipc/i3-derived and repins, so run it in a
scratch worktree and discard that worktree afterwards.

The run takes the host's oracle-sweep lock when ORACLE_SWEEP_LOCK names one,
so a sweep and a regeneration never share the machine.
Exit status: 0 done and validate passes; 1 a prerequisite or unit failed;
3 every unit agreed but validate fails (follow-up triage or README figures).
"""
